# G007 — Change Return Program

*v2. See `change.md` for prose: making change as priority-ordered
allocation against uneven denominations, same structure as covering
bills across a month against uneven due dates.*

---

## Choreographic Case: Monthly Bill Coverage

[monthly-bill-coverage @month
    IN ORDER TO
        cover each bill as it comes due with the cumulative P&L available
        and signal to trading whether scope-adjust is needed
        by treating bills as denominations and P&L as the amount

    @coverage <- [cover-obligations
                    {available: @month:cumulative-pnl,
                     bills: [
                        {name: "Captivate",    amount: 19,  due: 1}
                        {name: "Anthropic",    amount: 100, due: 10}
                        {name: "DigitalOcean", amount: 24,  due: 15}
                        {name: "ElevenLabs",   amount: 22,  due: 22}
                     ]}]

    <- @kathryn{evaluate @coverage}
        where all bills covered before their due dates
            -> #on-plan
        otherwise
            -> #prioritise-trading
]

---

## Verb Surface

[make-change
    {amount, denominations}                  ;; -> [coin count]
]

[cover-obligations
    {available, bills}                        ;; -> coverage map
]

---

## Distinctive Innate idiom: priority allocation `where` largest-first covers most

[make-change {amount: @cents, denominations: @denoms}]
    IN ORDER TO
        allocate @cents across @denoms largest-first
        emitting a count per denomination summing back to @cents

    remaining <- @cents
    for @d in @denoms ordered descending
        @count    <- remaining / @d (integer division)
        remaining <- remaining mod @d
        record (@d → @count)
    where remaining is zero   -> return allocation
    otherwise                  -> #cannot-make-exact-change
]

G005 introduced decision context; G006 introduced amortised `where`;
G007 connects them — bills are denominations, P&L is the amount,
cover-obligations is making change against a schedule.

---

## Demo

[demo
    -> [make-change {amount: 87, denominations: [25, 10, 5, 1]}]
    ;; -> {25: 3, 10: 1, 5: 0, 1: 2}

    -> [cover-obligations
          {available: 200,
           bills: [{amount: 100, due: 10}
                    {amount: 80,  due: 20}]}]
    ;; -> {covered: [both], remainder: 20}
]
